# R2RML Mapping Rules

- Each triples map has exactly one `rr:logicalTable` and one subject map.
- IRI `rr:template` values must match ontology URI patterns (`https://example.org/marine-life/...`).
- Use `rr:class` for `rdf:type` aligned with SHACL `sh:targetClass`.
- Literals: set `rr:datatype` or `rr:language`. Remember NULLs yield no triple.
- Relate tables with `rr:parentTriplesMap` + `rr:joinCondition`, or an `rr:sqlQuery` view when derivation is clearer in SQL.
- Target predicates must exist in `ontology/` (or be agreed temporary stubs).
- Do not invent vendor-specific mapping properties; stay on the `rr:` vocabulary from https://www.w3.org/TR/r2rml/.
